What are Audio Interfaces?
Audio Interfaces are specialized hardware devices that connect to computers via USB, Thunderbolt, or other interfaces to dramatically enhance audio input and output capabilities. They serve as the critical bridge between professional microphones, instruments, and studio monitors, providing the high-quality preamps, analog-to-digital converters (ADCs), and output connections necessary for professional recording, mixing, and content production.
